{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 39, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187 he was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. He played a significant role in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem during the 12th century. \n*Early Life* \nRaymond III was born around 1140 to Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. His father was the Count of Tripoli and his mother was the daughter of King Baldwin II of Jerusalem. \n*Reign* \nRaymond III became the Count of Tripoli in 1152 after the death of his father. He was around 12 years old at that time and the regency was held by King Baldwin III of Jerusalem. \n*Relationships and Alliances* \nRaymond III formed alliances with other Christian states in the region including the Byzantine Empire. He also formed alliances with Muslim states including the Zengid dynasty. \n*Military Campaigns* \nRaymond III participated in several military campaigns against the Muslim states in the region. He fought against Nur ad-Din Zengi the ruler of the Zengid dynasty. \n*Imprisonment and Later Life* \nRaymond III was imprisoned by Nur ad-Din Zengi in 1164 after being defeated in the Battle of Harim. He was released from prison in 1173 after paying a large ransom. \n*Succession Crisis* \nRaymond III played a significant role in the succession crisis of the Kingdom of Jerusalem after the death of King Amalric I in 1174. He supported the claim of Baldwin IV to the throne. \n*Death* \nRaymond III died in 1187 without an heir. The County of Tripoli was inherited by his nephew Raymond IV Count of Tripoli. \n*Legacy* \nRaymond III is remembered as a significant figure in the history of the County of Tripoli and the Kingdom of Jerusalem. He played a crucial role in the politics of the region during the 12th century. \n*Historical Records* \nThere are several historical records of Raymond III's life and reign including the works of William of Tyre and Ibn al-Athir. These records provide valuable information about the history of the County of Tripoli and the Kingdom of Jerusalem during the 12th century.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -9.775113539944869e-06}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " III", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.0009117737063206732}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.00015948931104503572}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.5847842693328857}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.4840473532676697}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -4.887569048150908e-06}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -9.417489309271332e-06}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": " from", "logprob": -0.05688214302062988}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -3.933898824470816e-06}, {"token": "115", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.006717361975461245}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -6.9141146923357155e-06}, {"token": "118", "logprob": -1.311301275563892e-06}, {"token": "7", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " he", "logprob": -0.17411643266677856}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.012860337272286415}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.14297272264957428}, {"token": " son", "logprob": -0.036696907132864}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Raymond", "logprob": -1.2516897186287679e-05}, {"token": " II", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.005363005213439465}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " H", "logprob": -0.00011419598013162613}, {"token": "odi", "logprob": -0.0024207117967307568}, {"token": "erna", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-0